WEBVTT

00:22.598 --> 00:27.241
The monitors are humming in the artificial

00:27.341 --> 00:28.021
light

00:31.904 --> 00:34.726
I've been staring at the ceiling through a

00:34.786 --> 00:37.408
never-ending night

00:41.102 --> 00:46.206
I can't feel the floor beneath me The gravity is

00:46.306 --> 00:47.246
gone

00:50.729 --> 00:56.473
Just a broken piece of metal Waiting for the dawn

01:00.168 --> 01:04.793
But I turn my heavy head and look across the room

01:05.173 --> 01:08.977
You're sleeping in the corner, a beacon in the

01:09.017 --> 01:13.021
gloom You didn't take the transport, you didn't

01:13.081 --> 01:17.506
fly away You planted down your boots and swore

01:17.546 --> 01:21.570
that you would stay The structural integrity's

01:21.630 --> 01:25.213
completely compromised But I can see the

01:25.333 --> 01:29.317
sanctuary reflecting in your eyes You cross the

01:29.437 --> 01:34.141
silent ward and you pull me to your chest Holding

01:34.181 --> 01:38.805
down the armor so the engine gets to rest You are

01:39.926 --> 01:45.031
the anchor's hold Keeping me from drifting out

01:45.251 --> 01:49.813
into the cold When the orbit was broken When the

01:49.853 --> 01:53.473
vessel was wrecked You wrapped your arms around

01:54.213 --> 01:59.534
The damage to protect A gravitational embrace

01:59.814 --> 02:04.455
In the middle of the dark Holding all the pieces

02:04.615 --> 02:08.596
Saving the spark I'm surviving the crash

02:08.696 --> 02:14.217
Because you wouldn't let me go You are the

02:14.497 --> 02:15.777
anchor's hope

02:24.325 --> 02:27.787
They're running the diagnostics, reading out

02:27.827 --> 02:33.510
the chart. They can fix the heavy machinery, but

02:33.590 --> 02:36.091
they cannot

02:37.332 --> 02:38.693
fix the heart. I

02:42.495 --> 02:46.517
was terrified of floating into the endless

02:46.597 --> 02:52.680
black, a ghost inside a machine that is never

02:55.583 --> 02:57.444
You're coming back

03:01.045 --> 03:04.246
But you're standing by the console, your hands

03:04.346 --> 03:09.008
upon the glass Refusing every order to let the

03:09.128 --> 03:14.030
moment pass You pull me in again, tighter than

03:14.090 --> 03:18.412
before We're fighting off the vacuum right here

03:18.572 --> 03:22.073
on the floor The structural integrity's

03:22.133 --> 03:25.695
completely compromised But I can see the

03:25.815 --> 03:29.737
sanctuary reflecting in your eyes You cross the

03:29.857 --> 03:34.499
silent ward and you pull me to your chest Holding

03:34.519 --> 03:37.621
down the armor so the engine gets to rest

03:40.793 --> 03:46.496
You are the anchor's hold Keeping me from

03:46.576 --> 03:50.819
drifting out into the cold When the orbit was

03:50.919 --> 03:54.281
broken, when the vessel was wrecked You wrapped

03:54.341 --> 03:59.685
your arms around the damage to protect A

03:59.765 --> 04:04.208
gravitational embrace in the middle of the dark

04:04.648 --> 04:09.191
Holding all the pieces, saving the spark I'm

04:09.251 --> 04:12.914
surviving the crash because you wouldn't let me

04:12.994 --> 04:17.998
go You are the anchor's host

04:36.184 --> 04:45.772
I can't feel my legs I can't feel the ground But I

04:45.812 --> 04:56.300
can feel your arms And I am safe and sound Are the

04:56.340 --> 05:00.666
anchors whole? Keeping me from drifting out

05:00.826 --> 05:05.452
into the cold When the orbit was broken, when the

05:05.492 --> 05:09.077
vessel was wrecked You wrapped your arms around

05:09.718 --> 05:14.442
the damage to protect The gravitational

05:14.462 --> 05:18.963
embrace in the middle of the dark Holding all the

05:19.063 --> 05:23.184
pieces, saving the spark I'm surviving the

05:23.284 --> 05:29.245
crash because you wouldn't let me go You are the

05:29.565 --> 05:34.386
anchor's hold Never

05:34.406 --> 05:40.028
let me go The gravitational embrace

05:42.825 --> 05:44.650
Holding me in place

